BT 1 0 0 1 0 68.5 Tm 16 TL /F4 11.5 Tf .14902 .215686 .184314 rg (The majority concluded that the Constitution does not confer a right to abortion. Its reasoning emphasized) Tj T* (constitutional text and history and rejected abortion as a right deeply rooted in the nation\222s history and) Tj T* (tradition. It also concluded that stare decisis, the principle of adhering to precedent, did not require) Tj T* (preserving ) Tj /F5 11.5 Tf (Roe) Tj /F4 11.5 Tf ( and ) Tj /F5 11.5 Tf (Casey) Tj /F4 11.5 Tf (. The majority applied rational-basis review and found Mississippi\222s asserted) Tj T* (interests sufficient to sustain the law against this constitutional challenge. [1]) Tj T* ET
